/// Terminal verdict of a settled headless run — the inputs of the gh-1603
/// exit-code policy: whether the run ended on an empty assistant completion
/// (an unfinished session: no final answer was ever produced) and the last
/// completed turn's stop reason.
extension AgentCliHeadlessExit on AgentCli {
  /// Whether the settled run ended on an EMPTY assistant completion (gh-1603)
  /// — an UNFINISHED session even though no error/abort was raised. A run
  /// that still settles on an empty completion after the headless nudge
  /// budget produced no final answer; error/aborted terminals keep their own
  /// exit codes ([_headlessExitCode]).
  ///
  /// Reads the visible transcript's last message — only valid BEFORE
  /// [_afterRun]: post-run compaction folds assistant turns out of the
  /// visible transcript (issue #413), so the probe runs right after the
  /// settle, before any fold.
  bool _settledOnEmptyCompletion() {
    final settledMessage = _agent.state.messages.lastOrNull;
    return settledMessage is AssistantMessage &&
        settledMessage.stopReason != StopReason.error &&
        settledMessage.stopReason != StopReason.aborted &&
        isEmptyAssistantCompletion(settledMessage);
  }

  /// The process exit code of a finished headless run (gh-1603): an
  /// unfinished session (empty settle after the nudge budget) prints the
  /// explicit [headlessIncompleteMarker] on the diagnostics channel and
  /// fails with 1 — a distinguishable failure for the bench adapter, never
  /// a silent exit 0. Otherwise the exit code describes the LAST completed
  /// turn's terminal outcome (captured from the turn events, not the
  /// visible transcript, which post-run compaction rebuilds — issue #413):
  /// the checkpoint fold drops the assistant turns entirely and the classic
  /// trim marker lands after the error stop; both used to mask a failed run
  /// as exit 0.
  int _headlessExitCode({
    required bool endedOnEmptyCompletion,
    required StopReason? terminalStopReason,
  }) {
    if (endedOnEmptyCompletion) {
      io.writeln(
        '$headlessIncompleteMarker the run ended on an empty model '
        'response — no final answer was produced; the task did not '
        'complete',
      );
      return 1;
    }
    return switch (terminalStopReason) {
      StopReason.error => 1,
      StopReason.aborted => 130,
      _ => 0,
    };
  }
```

